    <DataNode elementId="AT4G23660-MONOMER" textLabel="4-hydroxybenzoate nonaprenyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q93YP7" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">|FRAME: TAX-3702| produces a |FRAME: UBIQUINONE-9|, carrying a nine-isoprene tail. However, the enzyme that catalyzes the transfer of the prenyl side chain to the benzoquione frame is called |FRAME: AT4G23660-MONOMER|, since it is not specific to a particular tail length. When expressed in a &lt;i&gt;Saccharomyces cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; strain defective in the 4-hydroxybenzoate polyprenyl diphosphate transferase &lt;i&gt;COQ2&lt;/i&gt;, the protein encoded by the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana PPT1&lt;/i&gt; gene was shown to complement the mutation |CITS:[15604701]|. The enzyme was shown to be catalyze the prenylation of a wide range of prenyl substrates ranging from |FRAME:GERANYL-PP| (C&lt;sub&gt;10&lt;/sub&gt;) to |FRAME:CPDQT-22| (C&lt;sub&gt;50&lt;/sub&gt;) |CITS:[15604701]|. The gene is predominantly expressed in the flower cluster. Inactivation of the gene in |FRAME: TAX-3702| resulted in the arrest of embryo development at an early stage of zygotic embryogenesis |CITS: [15604701]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G23660-MONOMER" />
